5 1110 #uuid "c1f5d297-2d85-55e8-8686-c1c67cd8f3f9" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275456 1034 "overestimate" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275456 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533973 true] [17592186275456 1111 #uuid "2321c850-8d6e-5cdb-b1d2-aa0aa4eba56a" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275457 1034 "underestimate" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275457 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533973 true] [17592186275457 1111 #uuid "372694fc-ab4f-5700-a70e-724aeabc781e" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275458 1034 "exact value" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275458 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533973 true] [17592186275458 1111 #uuid "c56eb15b-ef97-52ce-9db2-fe4a2d8a8c03" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275459 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275460 13194139533973 true] [17592186275459 1089 "q-74348" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275459 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533973 true] [17592186275459 1100 "The following table shows the values of a continuous function $f(x)$ over the interval $[4,9].$\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $5.5$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $4$ | $6$ | $9.5$ |\n\nUse the right Riemann sum, with the three subintervals indicated by the data, to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ over the interval $[4,9].$" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275459 1113 #uuid "db39980f-8283-5ef8-83b5-f354ae931bda" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275459 1145 "In this case, we have $n=3$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is approximated as \n\n$$\nA≈f(5.5)Δ{x}_{1}+f(8)Δ{x}_{2}+f(9)Δ{x}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{x}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $x$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δx$'s.\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $5.5$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δx$ | $-$ | $1.5$ | $2.5$ | $1$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $4$ | $6$ | $9.5$ |\n\nFinally, we plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈4\\cdot 1.5+6\\cdot 2.5+9.5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6+15+9.5 \\\\  & =30.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275461 13194139533973 true] [17592186275460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275462 13194139533973 true] [17592186275460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275463 13194139533973 true] [17592186275460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275464 13194139533973 true] [17592186275460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275465 13194139533973 true] [17592186275460 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533973 true] [17592186275460 1041 "selection" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275460 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275461 13194139533973 true] [17592186275460 1110 #uuid "d2a99f58-21b0-5f70-be82-6f1b49360c42" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275461 1034 "30.5" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275461 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533973 true] [17592186275461 1111 #uuid "bc1cfce2-6c67-5656-87bc-be24f48eda93" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275462 1034 "29.25" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275462 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533973 true] [17592186275462 1111 #uuid "ddbba9c1-d208-5e0d-9a78-34e013b77432" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275463 1034 "32.55" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275463 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533973 true] [17592186275463 1111 #uuid "dc228cb9-000b-5a1b-be3b-3059a46fc7c9" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275464 1034 "34.5" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275464 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533973 true] [17592186275464 1111 #uuid "a9f63acf-8db0-5178-8632-91127264c441" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275465 1034 "31.25" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275465 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533973 true] [17592186275465 1111 #uuid "650f6364-88bd-507c-acb9-321b25deaf37" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275466 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275467 13194139533973 true] [17592186275466 1089 "q-86350" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275466 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533973 true] [17592186275466 1100 "The following table shows the velocity of a plane during a $20$-minute trip.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{minutes})$ | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v(t)\\,(\\text{kilometers/minute})$ | $17$ | $25$ | $27$ | $k$ | $18$ |\n\nIf the right Riemann sum approximation of the total distance traveled during this period has a value of  $450\\,\\text{km}$, what is the value of $k?$\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the velocity-time graph.*" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275466 1113 #uuid "fb378625-ff34-5649-9eb8-1bcb7d6bde31" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275466 1145 "The area $A$ under the curve $y=v(t)$ can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{v(5)+v(10)+v(15)+v(20)}})\\cdot {{Δt}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $v(t)$ at each point:\n\n| $t$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v(t)$ | $25$ | $27$ | $k$ | $18$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(25+27+k+18)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =5(k+70) \\\\  & =5k+350\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total distance traveled during the $20$ minute period. Since we are given that the right Riemann sum approximation of the total distance is $450\\,\\text{km},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5k+350 & =450 \\\\ 5k & =450-350 \\\\ k & =\\frac{100}{5} \\\\ k & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275468 13194139533973 true] [17592186275467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275469 13194139533973 true] [17592186275467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275470 13194139533973 true] [17592186275467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275471 13194139533973 true] [17592186275467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275472 13194139533973 true] [17592186275467 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533973 true] [17592186275467 1041 "selection" 13194139533973 true] [17592186275467 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275468 13194139533973